  "line": 23,
  "situation": "The ground of that appeal is God's own stated will, cited back to Him. *Who wilt have all men to be saved* (1 Timothy ii. 4) and *who wilt have no man perish* (2 Peter iii. 9) are set as a pair — two declarations of what God wills, entered as evidence against His justice and in favour of His mercy. The line above them is the disciples' *carest thou not that we perish?*, printed under Marc. iv. 28; the verse is iv. 38, and the volume cites it rightly at printed 286 and again at 294. Kept as printed, the third such figure in two leaves.",
