  "printed": "Is. xxiv. 16",
  "page": 376,
  "line": 2,
  "situation": "The volume's own earlier page is the key to this unmarked one. *Ariditas mea, ariditas mea! væ mihi!* is the shape of Isaiah's *my leanness, my leanness, woe unto me*, with the book's own noun set into it — and printed 335 is where that noun was fastened to that verse, in a brace reading *woe is me { for my dryness, [Is. xxiv. 16] / for my hardness of heart, / for the drought of my eyes, [Jer. ix. 1] }*. Two of the three come back on this leaf with no reference at all — the dryness here, the *fountain of tears* eight lines down. A concordance made from the plate's marks would join neither.",
