  ],
  "printed": "Is. xxxiii. 15",
  "page": 323,
  "line": 12,
  "situation": "This is the reference the volume elsewhere gets wrong, and here it is right. `*Job* xiv. 4` — *who can bring a clean thing out of an unclean?* — stands correctly on this page; at printed 406, where Part III makes its own confession out of the same material, the plate prints `*Job.* xiv. 14`, which is *if a man die, shall he live again?* Both stand as printed and neither is mended. The corroborating witness is the book itself, which is worth more than any conjecture, and it is now the fourth such case — with `Is. xxxiii. 15` against §37's `xxxviii. 15`, `Psal. cxxx. 30` against printed 297's `cxxx. 3`, and printed 25 confirming the reading at 409.",
  "source": "identified",
