  ],
  "printed": "Is. xxxviii. 15",
  "page": 297,
  "line": 21,
  "situation": "The volume proves another of its own misprints, and this is the fourth time. Here `*Psal.* cxxx. 3` is cited correctly for *if thou shouldest mark iniquities*; at printed 40 the same verse is cited `*Psal.* cxxx. 30`, in a psalm that has eight verses. Both stand as printed. The pattern is now well established — printed 25 confirming the reading at 409, §17 confirming `Job. xiv. 4` against Part III's `xiv. 14`, §37 confirming `Is. xxxviii. 15` — and it is worth more than any conjecture, because the corroborating witness is the book itself.",
